  "title": "Denmark CPR breach exposed data on 8.8 million people",
  "narration": "Denmark just confirmed a breach of its national population register affecting about 8.8 million records. The access path was a Danish company with legitimate permission to query the system. Unauthorized users abused that access to obtain names, addresses and CPR numbers at scale. That distinction matters: trusted access became the attack path. Authorities have blocked the company’s connection, notified the data regulator, and police are investigating. People with name-and-address protection were excluded from that part of the exposure. The lesson is simple: centralized identity systems are only as secure as every organization allowed to query them.",
